_s': 0.02, 'post_handover_s': 10.0, 'return_hold_s': 8.0, 'reposition': {'speed_m_s': 0.5, 'accel_m_s2': 0.5}, 'reference': 'Before the subject event the outgoing controller tracks one runner-published trajectory_setpoint (position ramp, velocity and acceleration feed-forward, constant yaw) starting from its own current target: classic through OFFBOARD, RAPTOR through its external trajectory_setpoint input. At the event the stream stops and the incoming controller uses its original mechanism: RAPTOR mode-entry reset holds the activation position/yaw with zero velocity; classic AUTO_LOITER brakes to the navigator loiter point.', 'baselines': "p1_baseline_classic: classic OFFBOARD motion then AUTO_LOITER (same takeover mechanism, no controller switch). p1_baseline_raptor: RAPTOR external-setpoint motion then the stream stops; after RAPTOR's 200 ms setpoint timeout it holds its position (same capture rule as mode entry, no reset or switch).", 'motor_saturation': {'upper': 0.999, 'lower': 0.001, 'note': 'actuator_motors control in [0,1]; upper/lower limit within 1e-3'}, 'motor_step_window_s': [-0.1, 0.5], 'motor_rms_window_s': [0.0, 0.5], 'motor_rms_definition': "RMS over [change, change+0.5 s] and the four motors of (run actuator_motors - in-batch baseline mean curve), zero-order hold on a 1 ms grid aligned at each run's actual change; baseline = same-controller baseline of the same condition in the same batch.", 'elimination_ratio_definition': '(N0 - Nx) / (N0 - baseline) per metric, from in-batch group means (motor step at change, max altitude loss, motor RMS deviation).', 'entry_check': {'value_tolerance': 1e-05, 'classic_command_max_age_ms': 50, 'teacher_forcing_check_window_s': 1.0, 'teacher_forced_min_fraction': 0.99}, 'exploration': {'failure_criteria': {'safety_envelope': 'any of tilt >= 45 deg, angular-rate component >= 8 rad/s, horizontal radius >= 10 m, altitude >= 8 m (frozen safety envelope; reaching the limit counts), or a runner safety abort', 'no_joint_